{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/912991-novice-and-a-needing-help","id":912991,"title":"Novice and a needing help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-12T14:12:50-07:00","id":912991,"title":"Novice and a needing help","content":"Hey all!<br /> <br /> I am a novice storyteller and i have a few questions about Vampire the Requiem 2nd edition and some of the material provided.<br /> <br /> Is the New Orleans book still usable or do I need to change stuff in it due to changes in the Vampire the Requiem 2nd and/or events in real life?<br /> <br /> Is there any module or book on how to introduce players to the Chronicles of Darkness universe as they play? I just think it would be neat so the players can just dive in without being inundated with information day one, and being expected to know it because their characters would know it. <br /> <br /> What are some common mistakes that new storytellers usually make that I should be aware of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11957-vexlight","name":"VexLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11957_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T16:04:10-07:00","id":913055,"title":"","content":"New Orleans was a very early supplement, so the tone and setting are definitely a bit different. It was also released before Hurricane Katrina happened, so it takes no account of that.<br /> <br /> For a good introductory module, The Resurrectionists SAS has a good little intro story, but I can't think of anything that has a concerted slow burn intro to CofD. The God-Machine Chromicle CAN be that, but it's a very specific setting detail. That being said, Vampire can work very well as a &quot;newly Embraced&quot; game.<br /> <br /> I would say the biggest mistake really new people make is being overly literal with the rules. CofD doesn't account for every situation, and sometimes the rules won't be what you need for the given circumstances. Don't sweat that. Favour expedience and story over crunch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T16:23:44-07:00","id":913064,"title":"","content":"I know this is going to be dumb sounding, but I am not a 100% sure how New Orleans changed after hurricane Katrina. Based on a cursory glance, it looks like things would have tipped in Prince Vidal's favor.<br /> <br /> Considering the majority of the population is Caucasian now and the french quarter still being fixed and repopulated that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11957,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11957-vexlight","user":"VexLight","date":". 06-12-2016, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11957-vexlight","name":"VexLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11957_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T16:29:00-07:00","id":913070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VexLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/912991-novice-and-a-needing-help?p=913064#post913064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is going to be dumb sounding, but I am not a 100% sure how New Orleans changed after hurricane Katrina. Based on a cursory glance, it looks like things would have tipped towards Prince Vidal's power.<br /> <br /> Considering the majority of the population is caucasian now and the french quarter still being fixed and repopulated that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you might have to do a bit more heavy lifting if you want to set things post-Katrina. I'm currently in a Vampire game set in New Orleans in the 20s, as a matter of fact, so I'm also interested to see what the consequences are, when and if we get there...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T16:34:32-07:00","id":913073,"title":"","content":"I will probably have to just use the pre-Katrina setting and let my players know ahead of time. I don't think I am qualified to judge or guess how things might have shifted this early in my storyteller career. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11957-vexlight","name":"VexLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11957_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T16:00:50-07:00","id":913706,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1459/Vampire-The-Requiem-Demo-Full\" target=\"_blank\">The first edition introductory quickstart</a> was designed as an introduction to the setting from the first night. It would need some conversion to second edition, and like <b>City Of The Damned: New Orleans</b> it's from early in the line.<br /> <br /> To run a modern New Orleans game without a lot of rewriting, look at real-world news about ongoing effects on the city, but you can assume that a decade after Katrina things have more or less settled down, at least for the city's vampires. If you want to shake things up a bit more, you could set some stories before and some after, and bring in some upheavals in the later section - maybe one of the power players is killed or driven into torpor, for example, or the players have their characters take major action during the chaos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T23:30:41-07:00","id":913907,"title":"","content":"Here's my thoughts on introducing the greater World of Darkness: use only what fits, and no more. Vampire has a delicate, sensuous feel to it, and throwing in the existential threats that follow werewolves and mages the God Machine can throw that completely off-course. If you use some other detailed splat, don't worry about capturing their nuances. Don't illuminate the Auspices of that werewolf pack if their purpose is just to inflict violence in the setting. Ignore the Order of that witch if all you need are vengeance curses. If it's useful to your story, by all means use it, but don't feel like you have to use ALL of it.<br /> <br /> Characters shouldn't expect to know anything, tbh. Vampires don't get a training packet and an orientation video. Elders don't know all the changeling courts, understand the Paths of willworkers, or even that demons exist. What vampires know is they are hungry, sun and fire will kill them, and what's in the dark is worse. If your players know the Covenants in their city and who calls the shots, they're about as well-informed as any neonate, and that's the perfect place to start them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T00:32:28-07:00","id":913936,"title":"","content":"I think there was a one shot scenario released prior to Blood &amp; Smoke. I think it was called something like &quot;Reap the Whirlwing.&quot; Anywho haven't played it myself but if it's anything like the other gameline intros it could be a great place to start. Plus if it's like the others I think it might be free to download on DriveThurRPG","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T00:42:25-07:00","id":913941,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114063/Reap-the-Whirlwind\" target=\"_blank\">Reap The Whirlwind</a>, the Second Edition quickstart (originally released before it was named Second Edition and was called <b>Blood And Smoke</b>) contains an adventure called Into The Void, in which a vampire ruler falls and the PCs have to stop the city's Kindred society tearing itself apart. Change some names and use a different introduction, and it could be used as a turning point for an ongoing game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T10:20:55-07:00","id":914182,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'll look into it. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11957-vexlight","name":"VexLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11957_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}